---
code: munge-name-invalid
when-fires: an emitted `<munged>__<role>` funcname is not a legal sh NAME (leading digit, dot, non-ASCII). oracle/reserved.rs lint_oracle_reserved_names.
why: ca-munge-charclass (24M §4b): a broken function name cannot ship — REFUSED. `{problem}` is `ShNameProblem::describe()`.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
中pkg__predict() { :; }

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
dorc lint findings (advisory; the machine format `--format=jsonl` is the stable surface):

oracle.sh:
  error[munge-name-invalid]: Dorc munges `\xc3\xa4\xc2\xb8\xc2\xadpkg` into the
  sh function name `\xc3\xa4\xc2\xb8\xc2\xadpkg__predict`, which is not a legal
  NAME: non-ASCII character `\xc3\xa4` (a NAME admits only ASCII
  letters/digits/`_`). A broken function name cannot ship; rename
  `\xc3\xa4\xc2\xb8\xc2\xadpkg` to spell only ASCII letters, digits, `_`, `.`,
  or `-`.
        [ oracle.sh:2:1
     2 | \xe4\xb8\xadpkg__predict() { :; }
       | \______________________/
  error[oracle-file-not-load-inert]: A `# dorc-lang/v0.2`-marked oracle file
  must be inert to load -- nothing but function definitions and static
  assignments at top level -- and this is the first item that does more. Move
  top-level work into a role function or into the book; an oracle file is loaded
  for its definitions, never run.
        [ oracle.sh:2:1
     2 | \xe4\xb8\xadpkg__predict() { :; }
       | \______________________/

